# Everything on this machine.
#
# The default, and the reason the quickstart needs no signup: a model on the operator's own hardware,
# reached across the container bridge. Nothing a person said leaves the machine, which is the claim
# this product makes and the only profile in which it is true without qualification.
#
# A value already exported wins over the one here, so a single setting can be changed for one run
# without editing this file:
#
#     make test-inference INFERENCE_PROFILE=local
#     TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL=something-else make test-inference
#
# ── THIS IS THE VIEW FROM THIS MACHINE, NOT FROM A CONTAINER ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# `localhost` is where a model on this machine is, for anything running on this machine — the test
# targets, a `go run`, a script. A container cannot use that name for the host and needs
# `host.docker.internal` instead, which is what compose.yaml already defaults to.
#
# So a profile is for the tools, compose has its own defaults, and neither needs the other. Using one
# for both was tried and produced `dial tcp: lookup host.docker.internal: no such host` on the target
# the profile was added for.
#
# Requires Ollama listening beyond loopback, or the container sees nothing:
#
#     OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 ollama serve
#     ollama pull qwen3.6:35b-a3b-mxfp8
#     ollama pull qwen3-embedding:4b-q8_0
#
# Measured here, 2026-09-11 (docs/36-extraction-models.md): qwen3.6:35b-a3b-mxfp8 holds the
# extraction contract, 19 of 19, with Ollama's default of thinking on. qwen3.8:27b-mxfp8 is unusable in
# this profile, but not because it cannot extract: with thinking on, no call returned inside the
# client's two minutes. With thinking off the same model family passes the whole corpus, and this
# profile has no way to switch it off. `make test-inference` is what says so, and it is what to run
# before changing this line.

TAISCE_INFERENCE_ENDPOINT=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_ENDPOINT:-http://localhost:11434/v1}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EXTRACTOR_MODEL:-qwen3.6:35b-a3b-mxfp8}
TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_EMBEDDING_MODEL:-qwen3-embedding:4b-q8_0}

# One host, so one entry. Host and port, never a URL.
TAISCE_INFERENCE_ALLOWLIST=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_ALLOWLIST:-localhost:11434}

# No key: a model on this machine has nobody to authenticate to.
TAISCE_INFERENCE_API_KEY=${TAISCE_INFERENCE_API_KEY:-}
